[
    {
        "content": "<p>To try to introduce myself to proving theorems in lean, I have proved the basic theorem from analysis:</p>\n<p>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>sup</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>sup</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sup A &lt; \\sup B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sup</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sup</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span>, then there exists an element <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b \\in B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> that is an upper bound for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>Here is the code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Classical</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">):=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elts</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Supremum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pf_upper_bound</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pf_least_upper_bound</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exercise_1_3_9</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubtypeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Supremum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sup_B</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Supremum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elts</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">byContradiction</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">not_exists</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">not_forall</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">not_le</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">forall_b_some_a_is_greater</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A_is_upper_bound_for_B</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some_a_is_greater</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">forall_b_some_a_is_greater</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some_a_is_greater</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf5</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf6</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gt_iff_lt</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf5</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf10</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pf_upper_bound</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">is_upper_bound</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf8</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf8</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf11</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_of_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf6</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf10</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf12</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pf_least_upper_bound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_A_is_upper_bound_for_B</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not_lt</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h5</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In case that isn't very readable, the approach I am taking is a proof by contradiction, where we assume that no <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b \\in B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> is an upper bound of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span>,  and use that to show that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>sup</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sup A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sup</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> is an upper bound for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span>, which contradicts the starting assumption.</p>\n<p>This typechecks, but I feel it could be done better so I have some questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>I wanted to pass subsets (or I guess subtypes) of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span></span></span></span> around, so I made the <code>SubtypeOf</code> struct to represent the type of subtypes of a type. This feels a little clunky. Is there a better / standard way to do this?</li>\n<li>I intentionally steered away from \"tactic magic\" by doing things like using <code>rw</code> instead of <code>simp only</code> when I could, and always <code>simp only</code> instead of <code>simp</code>. (I have nothing against magic, I just like to learn the magic-free way of doing things first). But even considering that, I'm pretty sure my proof isn't as idiomatic or nice as it could be. How can I improve my current proof?</li>\n<li>Sometimes <code>rw [foo]</code> would fail, but <code>simp only [foo]</code> would do the rewrites I wanted. Every <code>simp only</code> in the proof is a place where <code>rw</code> wouldn't work. How is <code>simp only</code> different from <code>rw</code>?</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 615725056,
        "sender_full_name": "Colin Phillips",
        "timestamp": 1786399913
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1185182\">Colin Phillips</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Help.20with.20an.20introductory.20analysis.20proof/near/615725056\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ol>\n<li>I wanted to pass subsets (or I guess subtypes) of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span></span></span></span> around, so I made the <code>SubtypeOf</code> struct to represent the type of subtypes of a type. This feels a little clunky. Is there a better / standard way to do this?</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Do you know about <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set#doc\">docs#Set</a></p>",
        "id": 615725795,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786400333
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, I must have missed it because I kept searching for things named subset or subtype.<br>\nThat is exactly what I needed, thank you!</p>",
        "id": 615727938,
        "sender_full_name": "Colin Phillips",
        "timestamp": 1786401458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>also, do you know about <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=upperBounds#doc\">docs#upperBounds</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsLUB#doc\">docs#IsLUB</a></p>",
        "id": 615729260,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786402221
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, I wanted to try to implement those things myself so I didn't check.<br>\nBut I think if I rewrote the proof to use those, that would force me to do things in a Mathlib style, which will probably show me a cleaner way of doing things overall. Thanks again!</p>",
        "id": 615732872,
        "sender_full_name": "Colin Phillips",
        "timestamp": 1786404380
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, do you know about <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathematics_in_lean/\">#mil</a> ? That might help out</p>",
        "id": 615788596,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1786434789
    }
]